        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): show run failures above composer",
        "body": "Closes #108498\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users whose active Control UI run fails would see the failure rendered as an assistant transcript message. The assistant avatar, identity, timestamp, and turn styling make an operational error look like agent-authored content.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis PR proposes moving terminal run failures into a neutral alert aligned with the chat composer. The alert preserves contextual recovery guidance and genuine streamed assistant output, while raw provider diagnostics remain server-side; its expandable section points operators to `openclaw logs --follow`.\n\nThe alert has no manual dismiss action. It clears when the user retries, changes sessions, or the Gateway adopts a new run.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRun failures no longer look like agent replies or pollute the conversation. Contextual error guidance remains visible above the composer, genuine partial or completed assistant prose remains in the transcript, and retrying clears stale failure state before the next run.\n\n## Evidence\n\n| Current behavior | Proposed in this PR |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Run failures rendered as assistant chat bubbles](https://bright-osprey-e3gj.here.now/current-behavior.png) | ![Proposed neutral full-width run failure alert above the composer, without a dismiss control](https://dreamy-essence-dyh8.here.now/after.png) |\n\n- Focused validation: 740 tests passed across Gateway, Gateway protocol, agent failure handling, and Control UI state/view suites.\n- Control UI i18n verification and `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Regression coverage includes transcript exclusion, partial and completed response preservation, tool-split streams, legacy error events, post-final errors, safe diagnostics, placement, width, and retry clearing.\n- Structured Codex autoreview: clean after addressing all accepted findings.\n- Browser E2E was not rerun during this review; the mocked browser regression remains in the PR and full CI is pending while the PR stays draft.\n\nAI-assisted: Yes. I reviewed the complete diff, understand the behavior, and validated it with focused tests and browser-focused regression coverage.\n",
